\pard\sa120\cf2\b\fs30 REDLYNX - a free, standalone browser\b0\fs22\cf1\par
\pard\sa80\cf1 Free, and staying free. No account, no subscription, no cloud, no company.\par
\pard\sb220\sa100\cf2\b WHY WINDOWS WARNED YOU\b0\cf1\par
\pard\sa80\cf1 This installer is not signed, and that is a deliberate choice.\par
\pard\sa80\cf1 A code-signing certificate costs a few hundred dollars a year, and nobody\par
\pard\sa80\cf1 reads your code for it. It proves who wrote the software - not that the\par
\pard\sa80\cf1 software is safe. Signed malware exists. Unsigned honest software gets a\par
\pard\sa80\cf1 scary warning. Paying for that on free software is not happening.\par
\pard\sa80\cf1 "Windows protected your PC" means "we do not know who made this". It does\par
\pard\sa80\cf1 not mean anything was found wrong with it. Click More info, then Run anyway.\par
\pard\sb220\sa100\cf2\b WHAT IT DOES\b0\cf1\par
\pard\li360\sa60\cf1 Blocks ads and trackers, using the same public filter lists uBlock Origin\par
\pard\li360\sa60\cf1 uses, including video ads on the large sites.\par
\pard\li360\sa60\cf1 Downloads media - video, audio and image galleries - with yt-dlp,\par
\pard\li360\sa60\cf1 gallery-dl and ffmpeg bundled in. Nothing to install, no website to paste\par
\pard\li360\sa60\cf1 a link into.\par
\pard\li360\sa60\cf1 Browses .onion sites. The Tor daemon ships inside; one button in the\par
\pard\li360\sa60\cf1 Anonymity panel starts it.\par
\pard\li360\sa60\cf1 Searches eleven independent indexes at once, including archives and\par
\pard\li360\sa60\cf1 crawlers that hold pages ordinary search will not show you.\par
\pard\li360\sa60\cf1 Reader mode, tab suspending, encrypted DNS, per-site permissions, and an\par
\pard\li360\sa60\cf1 address bar that corrects typos without changing what you typed.\par
\pard\sb220\sa100\cf2\b WHERE YOUR DATA LIVES\b0\cf1\par
\pard\sa80\cf1 On this machine, in one folder, in ordinary files:\par
\pard\li360\sa60\cf1 %APPDATA%\\Redlynx\\redlynx\par
\pard\li360\sa60\cf1 History, bookmarks and settings are plain files. Readable by you, and by\par
\pard\li360\sa60\cf1 anything else running as you - same as every browser.\par
\pard\li360\sa60\cf1 Saved logins are encrypted with Windows DPAPI, tied to your Windows\par
\pard\li360\sa60\cf1 account. Another account on the same PC cannot read them. If encryption\par
\pard\li360\sa60\cf1 is unavailable, Redlynx refuses to save the login rather than writing it\par
\pard\li360\sa60\cf1 in the clear, and tells you so.\par
\pard\li360\sa60\cf1 An AI API key, if you add one, is encrypted the same way.\par
\pard\sa80\cf1 Nothing syncs. There is no cloud, no account and no Redlynx server to sync\par
\pard\sa80\cf1 to. Delete that folder and everything Redlynx knows about you is gone.\par
\pard\sb220\sa100\cf2\b WHAT IT CANNOT DO\b0\cf1\par
\pard\li360\sa60\cf1 It cannot promise to be unhackable. No software can, and anyone claiming\par
\pard\li360\sa60\cf1 otherwise is selling something.\par
\pard\li360\sa60\cf1 It cannot patch itself in place. Pages are drawn by Chromium, which has\par
\pard\li360\sa60\cf1 security flaws found and fixed regularly, and a fix means replacing the\par
\pard\li360\sa60\cf1 whole application - Chrome works the same way. Redlynx can fetch that\par
\pard\li360\sa60\cf1 replacement when one is published, but nothing is installed behind your\par
\pard\li360\sa60\cf1 back: it asks, you decide, and it applies when you quit. Turn the check off\par
\pard\li360\sa60\cf1 in Settings and it never contacts anything.\par
\pard\li360\sa60\cf1 It cannot protect you from yourself. Blocking ads is not the same as\par
\pard\li360\sa60\cf1 blocking malware, and Tor hides where you are, not what you hand over.\par
\pard\li360\sa60\cf1 It cannot hide you from a site you log into. Signing in identifies you no\par
\pard\li360\sa60\cf1 matter which browser you used.\par
\pard\li360\sa60\cf1 It has been tested by one person on Windows. Expect rough edges nobody\par
\pard\li360\sa60\cf1 has hit yet.\par
\pard\sb220\sa100\cf2\b WHAT IT NEVER DOES\b0\cf1\par
\pard\li360\sa60\cf1 No telemetry, no analytics, no crash reports, no identifiers.\par
\pard\li360\sa60\cf1 No accounts, no sync, no cloud.\par
\pard\li360\sa60\cf1 No phone-home, and no server that belongs to Redlynx. The one exception is\par
\pard\li360\sa60\cf1 the update check, which asks GitHub for a version number - it can be turned\par
\pard\li360\sa60\cf1 off, and it carries nothing about you either way.\par
\pard\li360\sa60\cf1 No selling anything, because there is nothing collected to sell.\par
\pard\sa80\cf1 Two background connections exist, both public and both optional:\par
\pard\fi-180\li360\sa60\cf1 \bullet  Ad-blocking filter lists refresh from their publishers - the same public\par
\pard\li360\sa60\cf1 files every ad blocker downloads.\par
\pard\fi-180\li360\sa60\cf1 \bullet  One update check, thirty seconds after launch, asking GitHub for a\par
\pard\li360\sa60\cf1 version number.\par
\pard\sa80\cf1 Neither carries anything about you, and Settings can do both by hand instead.\par
\pard\sa80\cf1 Everything else happens only when you ask: your searches go to the engine you\par
\pard\sa80\cf1 chose, downloads to the site you are downloading from, and nowhere else.\par
\par
